# Which tests/ programs go on the SD card, one name per line.
#
# samples/*.bas all go, by glob - this list is only for the
# tests, which mostly exist for the host gates.  Three names
# appear in BOTH directories (port, pulse, settick) and are
# different programs: the sample is the board demo and wins,
# which is why it is staged second.  mkccimage.sh says so when
# it happens rather than resolving it quietly.
#
# Until this list existed the set was whatever two sync
# scripts and a few hand copies had left in hwtest: 21 names
# in fcc/sync-mmbc.sh, and five more (bitbyte, lscomms,
# onewire, posflush, spi) that nothing maintained at all.
bench.bas
bitbyte.bas
box.bas
circle.bas
circrnd.bas
fbdemo.bas
forktest.bas
imgfmt.bas
imgloop.bas
imgm1c.bas
imgtrip.bas
localheap.bas
lscomms.bas
onewire.bas
palette.bas
pixart.bas
posflush.bas
ripple.bas
rtest.bas
saveimg.bas
solar_eclipse.bas
sombrero.bas
spi.bas
t1.bas
tri.bas
wtest.bas
solar_eclipse.in
